Goal:
To view the cronjobs that are in the dir that they have specified and extract the password.

Connect:
ssh user@host -port

Approach:
. First would be to check the cronjob details that is in the dir they provided.
. Upon checking the dir and the cronjib corresponding to the level i found out that there was a 
  file that was automated.
. Veiwing what that file was executing i noticed that it was sending the password of the next 
  levl into another file.
. Revealing the password was easy after this information.
Command:
cd /etc/cron.d
cat cronjob_bandit22
cat /usr/bin/cronjob_bandit22.sh
cat /tmp/t7O6lds9S0RqQh9aMcz6ShpAoZKF7fgv

Result:
The password was revealed in the tmp directory inside of a file whose permission were modified.

Key-takeaway:
Introduction to cronjob and crontabs.
